{"path":"memory/null_memory_resource","title":"std::pmr::null_memory_resource","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::pmr::</span>null_memory_resource","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/null_memory_resource","section":"memory","kind":"page","summary":"Returns a pointer to a memory_resource that doesn't perform any allocation.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/memory_resource\">&lt;memory_resource&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx17\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/memory_resource\"><span class=\"kw712\">std::<span class=\"me2\">pmr</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">memory_resource</span></span></a><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> null_memory_resource<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx17\">(since C++17)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Returns a pointer to a <code>memory_resource</code> that doesn't perform any allocation.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value </h3>\n<p>Returns a pointer <code>p</code> to a static storage duration object of a type derived from <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/memory_resource\">std::pmr::memory_resource</a></span>, with the following properties:\n</p>\n<ul><li> its <code>allocate()</code> function always throws <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/new/bad_alloc\">std::bad_alloc</a></span>;\n</li><li> its <code>deallocate()</code> function has no effect;\n</li><li> for any <code>memory_resource</code> <code>r</code>, <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">p<span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>is_equal<span class=\"br0\">(</span>r<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> returns <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>r <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> p</span></code>.\n</li></ul>\n<p>The same value is returned every time this function is called.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\"><p>The program demos the main usage of <code>null_memory_resource</code>: ensure that a memory pool which requires memory allocated on the stack will NOT allocate memory on the heap if it needs more memory.</p>\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;array&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;cstddef&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;memory_resource&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;string&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;unordered_map&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"co1\">// allocate memory on the stack</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/container/array\"><span class=\"kw1275\">std::<span class=\"me2\">array</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/byte\"><span class=\"kw2658\">std::<span class=\"me2\">byte</span></span></a>, <span class=\"nu0\">20000</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> buf<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"co1\">// without fallback memory allocation on heap</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/monotonic_buffer_resource\"><span class=\"kw716\">std::<span class=\"me2\">pmr</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">monotonic_buffer_resource</span></span></a> pool<span class=\"br0\">{</span>buf.<span class=\"me1\">data</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>, buf.<span class=\"me1\">size</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>,\n                                             std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">pmr</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">null_memory_resource</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"co1\">// allocate too much memory</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/container/unordered_map\"><span class=\"kw1301\">std::<span class=\"me2\">pmr</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">unordered_map</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">long</span>, <a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string\"><span class=\"kw1245\">std::<span class=\"me2\">pmr</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">string</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> coll<span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>pool<span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">try</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n        <span class=\"kw1\">for</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/size_t\"><span class=\"kw107\">std::<span class=\"me2\">size_t</span></span></a> i <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"nu0\">0</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> i <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> buf.<span class=\"me1\">size</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"sy2\">++</span>i<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n            coll.<span class=\"me1\">emplace</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>i, <span class=\"st0\">\"just a string with number \"</span> <span class=\"sy2\">+</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string/to_string\"><span class=\"kw1272\">std::<span class=\"me2\">to_string</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>i<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n            <span class=\"kw1\">if</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>i <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> i <span class=\"sy2\">%</span> <span class=\"nu0\">50</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"nu0\">0</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n                <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/clog\"><span class=\"kw1778\">std::<span class=\"me2\">clog</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"size: \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> i <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"...<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n        <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">catch</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/new/bad_alloc\"><span class=\"kw698\">std::<span class=\"me2\">bad_alloc</span></span></a><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> e<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cerr\"><span class=\"kw1776\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cerr</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> e.<span class=\"me1\">what</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1774\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"size: \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> coll.<span class=\"me1\">size</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Possible output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>size: 50...\nsize: 100...\nsize: 150...\nstd::bad_alloc\nsize: 183</code></pre> \n</div>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"memory","title":"Memory management library"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::pmr::null_memory_resource","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++17. Returns a pointer to a memory_resource that doesn't perform any allocation."},{"label":"Return value","note":"Returns a pointer p to a static storage duration object of a type derived from std::pmr::memory_resource, with the following properties:"},{"label":"Example","note":"The program demos the main usage of null_memory_resource: ensure that a memory pool which requires memory allocated on the stack will NOT allocate memory on…"}]},"standards":["C++17"],"wordCount":220,"codeBlockCount":2}
